Subject: [PATCH 9/9] port: make sig_atomic_t atomic on WASIX

PostgreSQL declares its signal and latch flags volatile sig_atomic_t,
which is enough where one kernel-synchronised address space backs a
process. This port runs each process as a separate WebAssembly
instance over shared native pages, and plain volatile loads and
stores are not atomic between instances: racing SetLatch and
ResetLatch could lose the set.

The build force-includes this header before every translation unit.
It renames libc's underlying typedef while signal.h is read, then
exposes sig_atomic_t as _Atomic of it, asserting size, alignment and
lock-freedom, so every signal flag compiles to WebAssembly atomic
accesses without changing the libc or annotating call sites.

diff --git a/src/include/port/wasix_atomic_sigatomic.h b/src/include/port/wasix_atomic_sigatomic.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3e44af0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/include/port/wasix_atomic_sigatomic.h
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+/*-------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ *
+ * wasix_atomic_sigatomic.h
+ *    sig_atomic_t as a WebAssembly atomic, force-included at build time.
+ *
+ * Copyright (c) 2026, Ethan Jones
+ *
+ * IDENTIFICATION
+ *    src/include/port/wasix_atomic_sigatomic.h
+ *
+ *-------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ */
+#ifndef WASIX_ATOMIC_SIGATOMIC_H
+#define WASIX_ATOMIC_SIGATOMIC_H
+
+/*
+ * PostgreSQL relies on one kernel-synchronised address space per process
+ * to make volatile sig_atomic_t flags visible across its processes. Here
+ * every process is a separate WebAssembly instance over shared native
+ * pages, so the flags themselves must use WebAssembly atomic accesses.
+ *
+ * Rename libc's underlying typedef while signal.h is read, then expose
+ * sig_atomic_t as an atomic with the same representation.
+ */
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+#error "the atomic sig_atomic_t shim supports C only"
+#endif
+
+#define sig_atomic_t wasix_libc_sig_atomic_t
+#include <signal.h>
+#undef sig_atomic_t
+
+typedef _Atomic(wasix_libc_sig_atomic_t) sig_atomic_t;
+
+_Static_assert(sizeof(sig_atomic_t) == sizeof(wasix_libc_sig_atomic_t),
+			   "atomic sig_atomic_t must preserve the libc ABI size");
+_Static_assert(_Alignof(sig_atomic_t) ==
+			   _Alignof(wasix_libc_sig_atomic_t),
+			   "atomic sig_atomic_t must preserve the libc ABI alignment");
+_Static_assert(__atomic_always_lock_free(sizeof(sig_atomic_t), 0),
+			   "atomic sig_atomic_t must be lock-free in signal handlers");
+
+#endif							/* WASIX_ATOMIC_SIGATOMIC_H */
